  "wikitext": "{{PageDisplay}}\n[[File:Sheep.png|200px|left|Sheep]]\n\n{{Infobox\n |title = [[Animals|Animal]]\n |level = 16 • 26 • 42\n |price = 800 • 2,300 • 3,800\n |gives = {{Infoicon|wool|big|link=Wool}}\n |time = every 6 h\n}}\n'''Sheep''' are [[farm]] [[animals]] that produce [[wool]]. They are unlocked at [[experience]] level 16. They are the fourth type of farm animal unlocked in the game. Baby sheep are called [[Lamb|Lambs]], which are later unlocked in Level 25.\n\n{{Clr}}\n----\n==='''Appearance'''===\n<gallery widths=\"185\">\nFile:Sheep.png|Sheep\nFile:Sheep Walking.png\nFile:Sheep Full.png|Sheep Full\nFile:Sheep Hungry.png|Sheep Hungry\nFile:Sheep Summer.png|Sheep Summer\nFile:Sheep Summer Full.png|Sheep Summer Full\nFile:Sheep Winter.png|Sheep Winter \nFile:Sheep Halloween.png|Sheep Halloween\nFile:Sheep Halloween Full.png|Sheep Halloween Full\n</gallery>\n----\n==='''Alternate appearance'''===\n{{Main|Themes}}\nSheep wear themed clothes and accessories during summer, Halloween and winter.\n----\n==='''Buying'''===\n[[File:Sheep Pasture.png|150px|left|A sheep pasture]]\nSheep must be placed in [[Sheep Pasture|sheep pastures]] to be purchased. Pastures cost 300 {{Infoicon|coin}} each. They are unlocked at levels 16, 26 and 42. Each pasture can house five sheep.\n\nAt level 16 sheep cost 800 coins each; at level 26 2,300 coins; at level 42 3,800 coins.\n\nSheep and sheep pastures can be bought from the [[shop]].{{Infoicon|shop|bigger|link=Shop}}\n{{Clr}}\n----\n==='''Harvesting'''===\n[[File:Sheep Shears.png|150px|left|Shears]]\nWool can be sheared from sheep every 6 hours. Players can skip the wait by paying 8 [[diamond]]s per sheep. Players must then give sheep [[Sheep Feed|sheep feed]] to get another harvest.\n\nSheep feed is made of:\n{| border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"2\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"text-align: center; margin: .5em 0;\"\n|-\n|[[File:Soybean.png|75px|Soybean|link=Soybean]]\n|[[File:Wheat.png|75px|Wheat|link=Wheat]]\n|-\n|'''x1'''\n|'''x3'''\n|}\n\n{{clr}}\n----\n==='''Strategy tips'''===\n*It takes 30 minutes to make 3 units of [[Sheep Feed|sheep feed]]. You can easily collect all your wool and replenish your feed stock by the time the sheep are ready to be sheared again.\n* Wool can pretty regularly be found in the [[Daily Dirt]].\n* Feeding farm animals and harvesting wool are common tasks in [[Derby|derbies]].\n----\n==='''Easter egg'''===\nTapping the sheep pasture or making a rock explode scares the sheep, making them run from the perceived danger. In other circumstances sheep look nervous and easily frightened. This somewhat mimics their behavior in real life: sheep are quick to flee and panic, and are sensitive to noise.\n----\n==='''Did you know?'''===\n* Where you tap hungry sheep, they turn into their full appearance. This only happens when you don’t have enough food to feed them. It lasts about 3 seconds.\n* The ghost costume sheep wear during Halloween is alike [http://disney.wikia.com/wiki/Jacob_Marley Jacob Marley's] in the Disney adaptation of Dickens's ''A Christmas Carol''.\n----\n\n{{Navigation}}\n{{Languages\n|de = Schaf\n|es = Oveja\n|fr = Mouton\n|it = Pecora\n|no = Sau\n|ru = Овца\n|sv = Får\n}}\n[[pt-br:Ovelha]]\n\n[[Category:Farm Animals]]",
